{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgxouxuq04","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Graph auto commit hook must be agent based not pure git","summary":"User requires the .graph post-commit auto-commit hook to use an AGENT (claude) to SELECT which files are relevant to commit — NOT a mechanical `git add .graph/*.jsonl`. Rationale (user, verbatim intent): \"we need agent to look for the relevant things to commit, no pure git can do.\" So the documented claude-based hook (backgrounds `claude --dangerously-skip-permissions -p ...` per commit to stage+commit the relevant .graph snapshot) is the INTENDED design — do not substitute a pure-git hook. This ships in the @zonoid/cli installer (graphAutocommitHookScript), off by default, armed via `--graph-autocommit` / ORCH_GRAPH_AUTOCOMMIT=1; merged to main at 3afae91. GOTCHA: arming it is blocked by the Claude Code auto-mode safety classifier (flags it as Create-Unsafe-Agents + Unauthorized-Persistence) — an agent cannot self-enable it even with chat authorization; the USER must run the enable command themselves or add a Bash permission allow-rule. Pure-git was offered and explicitly rejected.</summary>\n<parameter name=\"category\">preference","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T17:46:36.834Z","vec":[-0.07089027762413025,0.037492960691452026,-0.03948986530303955,-0.027089621871709824,0.0053290873765945435,-0.041215214878320694,-0.0045486814342439175,0.06174386665225029,-0.00783336441963911,0.07928808778524399,0.04833288490772247,-0.03432921692728996,0.05251193419098854,0.055143266916275024,0.04627391695976257,0.020268408581614494,0.04149690270423889,-0.04929855093359947,-0.01890568807721138,-0.003955664578825235,-0.03889916092157364,-0.030942706391215324,0.09668280929327011,0.0030755135230720043,0.09605492651462555,-0.08545293658971786,-0.06367222964763641,0.008313057944178581,0.03781948983669281,0.032686565071344376,0.01751953735947609,0.052195604890584946,0.0011421118397265673,0.0506163127720356,0.028158731758594513,0